course: dictionary
lesson: 221
title: Alike: the same, or nearly the same
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: When two things are alike, they are very similar. «The twins look alike» means you could almost mix them up. Alike is about how things are the same, and it is the opposite of different.
explain: Alike can also tell you how someone does something. «Treat everyone alike» means treat everyone in the same way, with no one getting special treatment. Here alike comes after the verb and tells you how.
explain: Alike can also mean "both" or "equally". «Adults and children alike» means adults and children both, in the same way. Check by swapping in "both": the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Alike usually comes after a noun or a verb, not before a noun. You say «the twins look alike», not «the alike twins». When you need a word before a noun, use similar or the same instead.
fact: Alike means very similar, looking or being almost the same.
fact: «The twins look alike» means the twins look almost the same.
fact: «Treat everyone alike» means treat everyone in the same way.
fact: «Adults and children alike» means both adults and children.
fact: A good check is to swap in "the same" or "both" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The twins look alike.» What does alike mean here? | Far apart | Shouting loudly | Very tall | *Very similar, almost the same
exercise: In science, Ben compares two leaves. Which sentence uses alike correctly? | Alike leaves the tree quickly. | *The two leaves are alike in shape. | The leaves alike were green and bright. | The alike leaves fell from the tree.
exercise: «Sadness is a normal feeling for everyone, boys and girls alike.» What does alike mean here? | Sadly | *Both boys and girls, in the same way | Only boys | Angrily
test: «Telling a trusted adult is the rule that works best, for boys and girls alike.» What does alike mean here? | Very quickly | Only for girls | *Equally, for both | Not at all
test: Which word completes the saying: «Great minds think ___»? | *Alike | Loudly | Sadly | Apart
exam: Which sentence uses alike correctly? | The alike path was dark. | Alike the children ran home. | *Children who leave the path get lost, because the trees all look alike. | They alike ran home fast.
